{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 10, :comments ["<b>And he became her son.</b> Like \"and these are the sons of Michal, Zerubbabel son of Shealtiel\" (Ezra 3:2, Haggai 1:1) — but he was the son of Pedaiah, brother of Shealtiel; because he raised him, he was called his son." "The name Moses is translated from the Egyptian language into the sacred language, and his name in Egyptian was Monius, and thus it is written in the Book of the Cult of the Earth, which was translated from the Egyptian language into the language of the Kedarites, and likewise in the books of the sages of Greece. Perhaps Pharaoh's daughter learned our language, or she asked — and do not be surprised that it is not a Hebrew name, for names are not preserved like verbs."], :book :exodus, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 2, :notes {0 "Ibn Ezra quotes Ezra 3:2, which reads 'sons of Shealtiel' in some versions; the phrase 'בני מיכל' is his interpretation of that verse, not a direct quotation."}, :source-witnesses [["Piotrkow, 1907-1911" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH990020973480205171/NLI"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:31:02.541851848Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}